    "checks": [
      "Accessory in-law dwelling (Use 91) is a use by right in R-1, R-2, R-3 and R-4 (27-401, 27-501, 27-601, 27-701). Zoning permit, no hearing",
      "Only relatives of the family living in the house may live there. It 'shall not be used as a rental unit' (27-1793.1.C, H)",
      "Only in a single-family detached dwelling, on a lot of at least 9,000 sq ft. One per lot (27-1793.1, A, C)",
      "The unit is part of the house or in an existing accessory structure such as a garage that sits inside the district building envelope, that is outside all required yards (27-1793.1.D, 27-2104)",
      "A new separate building for the unit needs a lot 1.5 times the district minimum: R-1 30,000, R-2 18,750, R-3 and R-4 13,500 sq ft (27-1793.1.D)",
      "No basement unit unless one wall is at grade with direct outside access. No exterior change that makes the house look like more than one dwelling (27-1793.1.E, F)",
      "The accessory building may not be taller than the house (27-1793.1.G). Accessory structures are capped at 20 ft and 500 sq ft of ground floor area (27-1786.1.D, G)",
      "A Bucks County Department of Health permit (public sewer or adequate septic) is needed before the zoning permit (27-1793.1.B)",
      "27-1793 sets no floor area cap and no owner occupancy rule",
      "Parking: two spaces per dwelling unit for residential uses, garage spaces do not count (27-2200.1.C). The code does not say whether the in-law dwelling counts as a dwelling unit",
      "R-3 and R-4 allow a two-family (semidetached) dwelling by right (27-601, 27-701)"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Warminster Township, Department of Licenses and Inspections (named in 27-1786.1.B). Township site not opened. The Chapter 'Housing' of the Township code was not read."
  },
